Q1. What are Design Patterns?
Why do we need them?

Interview Ready Answer

Design Patterns are proven and reusable
design solutions for commonly occurring
software design problems.

They are NOT ready-made code.

They are templates or guidelines
that help developers design software
efficiently.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why were Design Patterns introduced?

Developers were solving the same software
design problems repeatedly.

Instead of reinventing the solution every time,

the Gang of Four (GoF) documented
proven solutions that can be reused
across different projects.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Design Patterns?

• Reduce Tight Coupling.
• Improve Maintainability.
• Improve Reusability.
• Improve Scalability.
• Improve Readability.
• Make Testing Easier.
• Provide Standardized Solutions.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

Architects use building blueprints
instead of designing every building
from scratch.

Similarly,

Developers use Design Patterns
as proven blueprints for software design.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Examples

Singleton Pattern

↓

Only one Logger or Database Connection.

Factory Pattern

↓

Creates objects without exposing
object creation logic.

Builder Pattern

↓

Creates complex objects step by step.

