Q2. Who are the Gang of Four (GoF)?
How are Design Patterns classified?

Interview Ready Answer

The Gang of Four (GoF) are four software
engineers who published the famous book

"Design Patterns:
Elements of Reusable Object-Oriented Software"

in 1994.

The four authors are

• Erich Gamma
• Richard Helm
• Ralph Johnson
• John Vlissides

They documented

23 Design Patterns

which are divided into

3 Categories.

------------------------------------------------------------

1. Creational Patterns

Purpose

Object Creation.

Examples

• Singleton
• Factory Method
• Builder

------------------------------------------------------------

2. Structural Patterns

Purpose

Combining Classes and Objects.

Examples

• Adapter
• Decorator
• Proxy

------------------------------------------------------------

3. Behavioral Patterns

Purpose

Communication between Objects.

Examples

• Observer
• Strategy
• Command

------------------------------------------------------------

Memory Trick

Creational

↓

Create Objects

----------------------------

Structural

↓

Connect Objects

----------------------------

Behavioral

↓

Communicate Objects

